{
  "_note": [
    "The reference's admission answers on BOTH receive paths, captured once and committed.",
    "This file is the expectation the ledger row's `Reference route` cell is compared against",
    "(otlp_prom_translation::the_admission_row_names_every_route_the_reference_was_measured_on),",
    "so the row cannot name a route the reference was never asked on and cannot omit one it was.",
    "",
    "WHAT IT CANNOT DO. It fixes what the reference did on one date at one image digest. No CI",
    "job re-captures it, so a later reference release that moves the boundary will not be noticed",
    "here. Editing a value below to match a shortened ledger row without re-running the procedure",
    "defeats the gate; the `revision` and `captured` fields are what a reviewer checks that",
    "against.",
    "",
    "TWO ANCHORS. `boundary` and `body_lines` were taken with the head at the wall clock, where",
    "the past bound (head.maxTime - 60 min) and the future bound (wall clock + 10 min) coincide.",
    "`future_anchor` is the measurement that separates them: the head was warmed AHEAD of the",
    "clock and the future cutoff did not follow it."
  ],
  "procedure": [
    "podman run -d --name <unique> -p <port>:9090 docker.io/prom/prometheus@sha256:0e698e35e50d1ddc2d11a4a55b089fe62eb71358a5c204dfafd21bdf8ffe04b8",
    "  --config.file=/etc/prometheus/prometheus.yml --storage.tsdb.path=/prometheus",
    "  --web.enable-remote-write-receiver --web.enable-otlp-receiver",
    "The stock config self-scrapes, which is what anchors the head at the wall clock.",
    "Read the clock once per table with GET /api/v1/query?query=vector(time()) and the head's",
    "maximum with GET /api/v1/status/tsdb (data.headStats.maxTime).",
    "remote write: POST /api/v1/write, Content-Type application/x-protobuf,",
    "  Content-Encoding snappy, X-Prometheus-Remote-Write-Version 0.1.0, body a v1",
    "  prompb.WriteRequest with one series and one sample per rejected series.",
    "OTLP: POST /api/v1/otlp/v1/metrics, Content-Type application/json, body an",
    "  ExportMetricsServiceRequest with one gauge data point per emitted series and a",
    "  per-run service.name (target_info is resource-level and a repeat run collides).",
    "Offsets are measured from the clock read; `boundary` rejections do not move the head, so",
    "the negative offsets are taken before the positive ones."
  ],
